{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966783,"nonce":"Tx04ka2gD8sNK19Yd5JGPsSOKnk=","title":"CI ran cargo check/clippy --workspace --all-features but never --all-targets, so no example","message":"`cargo check --workspace --all-features` builds **lib and bin targets\nonly**. Examples need `--all-targets` (or `--examples`). CI had the\nformer, so every example in the repo went uncompiled indefinitely.\n\nHow it surfaced: a `cn::sidebar` signature change (`content` losing its\n`active_item` argument) broke `examples/blinc_app_examples/examples/\ncn_demo.rs`, and CI stayed green through it. The break was only found by\nrunning the example by hand.\n\n**The wrong diagnosis, worth remembering.** The obvious explanation is\n`required-features = [\"cn\"]` on the `cn_demo` target plus `blinc_cn`\nbeing an optional dep — i.e. a *feature* gap. That is not it: CI already\npassed `--all-features`. Proven by deliberately breaking `cn_demo` and\nrunning both forms: plain `--all-features` reported 0 errors,\n`--all-targets` caught it at once. Verify which flag is missing rather\nthan assuming it is the feature one.\n\nFixed by adding `--all-targets` to both the `cargo check` and the\n`cargo clippy` steps in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. The workspace passed\nwith it enabled, so it did not redden the build.\n\nNote `cargo nextest run --workspace --all-features` builds test targets\nbut still not examples, so the test job never covered this either.","files":null}]}